title Keep the field -- grain-incense would be a birth, not a rename
prompt Keaton asked whether ~/grain should be ~/grain-incense for consistency with grain-furrow and grain-harvest.
think The three loop directories would read more evenly as grain-incense, grain-furrow, grain-harvest. The field is a different name: SOURCE clones ~/grain, the jail writes it, birth_a_clone runs from it, sibling gpg.program paths point at its wrapper. Asked this morning at 170513; the sitting was keep the field, map mind to furrow.
think Two shapes. Birth ~/grain-incense with birth_a_clone.rish: unattended incense loop gets its own tree, GUI sitting stays in the field, tree-match wants grain-incense, two writers stop sharing one checkout. Rename the field: checkpoint, inbound sweep, SOURCE and jail and every absolute sshCommand -- his word, not a kg.
obs Do not rename ~/grain without that word. Birth is the mechanical door if he wants the seat-named tree.
file tools/l/birth_a_clone.rish the birth recipe, destination grain-incense
